IMPORT prelude

-- Wyoming income tax, Wyoming Statutes Title 39 chapters 7 and 12 -- the whole of Wyoming's income tax law, which imposes none:
-- W.S. 39-7-101 ("Repealed By Laws 1998, ch. 5, s 4.") and W.S. 39-12-101 (the state preempts the field of income and
-- earnings taxes, so no county, city, town or other political subdivision may impose one).
--
-- SEAT: the individual who lives or works in Wyoming ("Do I owe Wyoming income tax? May my city or county tax my wages?").
--
-- Edition: the Legislative Service Office's title 39 PDF (created 2026-10-14), downloaded 2026-10-19T18:00:49Z, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/wy-stat-39-ch07-ch12.txt (unofficial).
--
-- What Wyoming does give individuals by way of tax relief (the refund for residents 65 or over or totally disabled, W.S.
-- 39-11-109(c)) is encoded beside this, in ../../../wyoming-statutes-title-39-taxation-and-revenue-chapter-11-administration/
-- encodings/baseline-2026-10/. Federal income tax still applies (subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986/).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Wyoming income tax -- W.S. 39-7-101, 39-12-101`

-- W.S. 39-7-101: "Repealed By Laws 1998, ch. 5, s 4." Chapter 7 (Income Taxes) has no other section, and chapter 12 imposes no
-- tax: no provision of the deposited text levies a state tax on an individual's income.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the state imposes an income tax on individuals` IF FALSE

-- W.S. 39-12-101: "The state of Wyoming does hereby preempt for itself the field of imposing and levying income taxes, earning
-- taxes, or any other form of tax based on wages or other income and no county, city, town or other political subdivision shall
-- have the right to impose, levy or collect such taxes."
DECLARE `Who would levy it` IS ONE OF
    `the state`
    `a county`
    `a city or town`
    `another political subdivision`

DECLARE `Local tax answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: the state keeps the power to tax income but levies no income tax (W.S. 39-12-101; 39-7-101 repealed)`
    `no: the field is preempted by the state, and no county, city, town or other political subdivision may impose, levy or collect such a tax (W.S. 39-12-101)`

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who would levy it`
GIVETH A `Local tax answer`
`whether it may tax wages or other income` `who` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the state` THEN `no: the state keeps the power to tax income but levies no income tax (W.S. 39-12-101; 39-7-101 repealed)`
    OTHERWISE `no: the field is preempted by the state, and no county, city, town or other political subdivision may impose, levy or collect such a tax (W.S. 39-12-101)`

§ `Questions for the individual`

@export Do I owe Wyoming state income tax on my wages or other income? (No: W.S. 39-7-101 is repealed and nothing else levies one.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I owe Wyoming income tax` IF
    `the state imposes an income tax on individuals`

@export Does the state, or may a Wyoming county, city, town or other local government, tax my wages or other income (W.S. 39-12-101)?
GIVEN `which government` IS A `Who would levy it` @desc Which government would levy the tax: the state, a county, a city or town, or another political subdivision
GIVETH A `Local tax answer`
`Can this government tax my wages` `which government` MEANS
    `whether it may tax wages or other income` `which government`
